{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "Sally in the UK", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "On the Bus", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 11, "type": "position"}, {"content": "scholar > Famous Structures > Buckingham Palace", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 8, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A2.1", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": " Accurately use information about travel and vacations in social situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": " Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": " Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": " Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": " Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": " Gives appropriate directions to places taking into account the type of interlocutor.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": " Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": " Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_8"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"content": "engenn4le08ob11re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "picture ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "photograph ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: If you want to take a few more pictures, please feel free.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le08ob11aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": " These are words you use when you visit a new place.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Prepositions of Place", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "When you say where things are, you use prepositions of place like <span class=\"italic\">along, through, across, on, at, inside, outside</span> or <span class=\"italic\">around</span>.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":9,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class =\\\"strong\\\"> Preposition </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class =\\\"strong\\\"> Use </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class =\\\"strong\\\"> Example </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" in \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" a room, a city\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" See the fine antique furniture and works of art in the State Rooms?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"on \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" a street, a river bank\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" The museum is on the south bank.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"through \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" a open area, like a park or a market\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" You can walk through the market.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"across \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" a street, a river\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" The bridge goes across the River Thames.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"inside \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" a building\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" That means the Queen is inside the building.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"outside \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" a building\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Did you notice the Royal Standard outside the palace?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"around \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" outside a building\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" You can see the beautiful 40-acre garden and lake around the palace.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"along\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" beside a path or a river\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" I loved walking along the River Thames.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": " Near - Far", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You can use the adjectives <span class =\"italic\">near, close</span> and <span class =\"italic\">far</span> to say the distance of one thing or place to another.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "How far is it?<br /> It's about 10 miles away. <br />It's about 40-minute walk.<br /> That's too far to walk.<br /> The Underground is close.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">Near</span> and <span class=\"italic\">close</span> have the same meaning. <span class=\"italic\">Far</span> has the opposite meaning.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The expression too <span class=\"italic\">far</span> means something is very far in a negative way.", "type": "text"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "prehistoric ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "dating from the time before writing ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Stonehenge is the most famous prehistoric monument in the world.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le08ob11aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "stone ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "material that comes from the ground ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: What kind of stones are they?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le08ob11aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "excursion ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a short trip ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It's a 10-hour excursion to Stonehenge.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le08ob11aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "famous ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "many people know about it ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Not too far from there is Tower Bridge, a very famous bridge.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le08ob11aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "technology ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "ideas and equipment to improve they way we live ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Ancient people built huge monuments with very little technology.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le08ob11aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Do a search online for words and expressions people use in texting.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write a list of 20 words and expressions. For each one, explain what it means using normal words.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write a funny text message conversation using the short forms.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Practice reading the dialogue with a partner.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"content": "I identify 20 short forms of words or expressions online.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write the meanings of short forms used in conversations.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write a text message conversation using short forms.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I practice the dialogue with a partner.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"type": "welcome", "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "id": 0, "template_override": 1}, {"title": "", "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "engenn4le08ob11re2aud01", "images": [{"image": "engenn4le08ob11re2img05.jpg", "id": 0, "time": "0", "text": ""}, {"image": "engenn4le08ob11re2img05.jpg", "id": 1, "time": "100", "text": "<span class =\"strong\">John</span>:  Hey, Sally! What's up?<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Sally</span>: I'm great! I'm coming back from Stonehenge. It's an outdoor prehistoric structure made of 30 huge stones. They built it with no technology. <br />\n<span class =\"strong\">John</span>: How did they do that?<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Sally</span>: I don't know. It's a very famous mystery."}, {"image": "engenn4le08ob11re2img05.jpg", "id": 2, "time": "19000", "text": "<span class =\"strong\">John</span>: How far is it from London?<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Sally</span>:  It's about 90 miles away, or 145 kilometers. It's a very interesting excursion to Stonehenge.<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">John</span>: Where are you now?<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Sally</span>: I'm on a bus. I'm going back to London. We go straight on this road for about 1 hour. Then we turn right at an intersection."}, {"image": "engenn4le08ob11re2img01.jpg", "id": 3, "time": "43000", "text": "<span class =\"strong\">John</span>: The cruise ship is heading to Guatemala. We stop there, then we go to Belize. Where are you going next?<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Sally</span>: I'm going to the Salzburg Festival in Austria.<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">John</span>: Awesome!"}], "coverimg": "engenn4le08ob11re2img05.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "audio", "id": 3}, {"title": "", "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "engenn4le08